    </dashboard>
    <dashboard name='Story 1' type='storyboard'>
      <layout-options>
        <title>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1f3a5f' fontname='Tableau Bold'>Bondora Credit Risk: Where do defaults come from? (2023–2025)</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </title>
      </layout-options>
      <style>
        <style-rule element='story-description'>
          <format attr='font-size' value='16' />
          <format attr='color' value='#1f3a5f' />
          <format attr='background-color' value='#00000000' />
        </style-rule>
        <style-rule element='story-point-caption'>
          <format attr='width' value='160' />
        </style-rule>
      </style>
      <size maxheight='1000' maxwidth='1600' minheight='1000' minwidth='1600' sizing-mode='fixed' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='2' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone h='98400' id='1' param='vert' removable='false' type-v2='layout-flow' w='99000' x='500' y='800'>
            <zone h='3300' id='3' type-v2='title' w='99000' x='500' y='800' />
            <zone h='10100' id='4' is-fixed='true' paired-zone-id='5' removable='false' type-v2='flipboard-nav' w='99000' x='500' y='4100' />
            <zone h='85000' id='5' paired-zone-id='4' removable='false' type-v2='flipboard' w='99000' x='500' y='14200'>
              <flipboard active-id='15' nav-type='caption' show-nav-arrows='true'>
                <story-points>
                  <story-point caption='Finland dominates (66% of loans)' captured-sheet='Loans per Country' id='1' />
                  <story-point caption='Lending more than doubled from 2023 to 2025' captured-sheet='Loans per Year' id='2' />
                  <story-point caption='The rating works: AA 5.5% → G 26.5%' captured-sheet='Rating' id='3' />
                  <story-point caption='Spain, Latvia and Denmark default far above average' captured-sheet='Country' id='4' />
                  <story-point caption='Low income (under 1,500 EUR) doubles the risk' captured-sheet='Income' id='5' />
                  <story-point caption='37–60-month loans are the riskiest' captured-sheet='Duration' id='6' />
                  <story-point caption='Loans at 25%+ interest: 1 in 4 defaults' captured-sheet='Interest' id='7' />
                  <story-point caption='Defaulted borrowers earn less and borrow more' captured-sheet='Defaulted Vs Not' id='8' />
                  <story-point caption='Combining factors finds the riskiest loans' captured-sheet='Rating x Duration' id='10' />
                  <story-point caption='All risk drivers at a glance rating, income and interest rate' captured-sheet='Risk Overview ' id='15' />
                  <story-point caption='Recommendations' captured-sheet='' id='16' />
                  <story-point caption='Limitations' captured-sheet='' id='17' />
                </story-points>
              </flipboard>
            </zone>
          </zone>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#444444' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='8' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' forceUpdate='true' h='78300' hidden='true' id='8' story-point-id='16' type-v2='text' w='73000' x='12438' y='15400'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Recommendations</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000'>1. Check weak ratings more strictly. F- and G-rated loans default 25.5–26.5%, almost 5× more than AA loans (5.5%). Unrated loans also default above average (16.7%).</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000'>2. Don’t rely on the rating alone in Latvia. Even A-rated Latvian loans default 30%, more than G-rated loans overall (26.5%). Add a country-level check to the approval.</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000'>3. Price the risk in Spain and Denmark. Spain defaults 51.5% and Denmark 29.7%, but their interest rate is only about 18–20%. Raise rates or tighten approval; in Spain, almost all loans are unrated.</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000'>4. Watch weak ratings combined with long loans. G-rated 13–36-month loans (29.7%) and F-rated 37–60-month loans (27.6%) are the riskiest combinations. Offer shorter terms or extra checks for ratings C–G.</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000'>5. Use income and interest rate as early-warning signs, and track the 12-month default rate. </run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000'>6. Income under 1,500 EUR (19.6%) and interest of 25%+ (24.7%) mean about twice the risk. The 12-month rate allows a fair comparison between years.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' forceUpdate='true' h='72500' hidden='true' id='9' story-point-id='17' type-v2='text' w='75750' x='12438' y='19400'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Limitations</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#1b1b1b'>1.  Association, not cause. The results show which groups default more, not why.</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#1b1b1b'>2. Young loans. 2025 loans have had less time to default, so their final default rate will rise. For a fair comparison we use the 12-month default rate (10.9%, 8.2%, 8.9%).</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#1b1b1b'>3. Small groups. Spain (1,578 loans) and groups under 100 loans, such as HR (19 loans), give less stable rates and were not interpreted.</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#1b1b1b'>4. Cancelled loans (4.1%) are counted as not defaulted. Without them, the default rate is 14.3% instead of 13.7%.</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#1b1b1b'>5. Few borrower details. The data has only country, income and rating, with no age, job or other debts. Columns known only after a default (e.g. months_in_default) were not used, to avoid leakage.</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#1b1b1b'>6. Peer-to-peer lending. Bondora’s borrowers and interest rates differ from a traditional bank’s, so the results do not transfer directly to banks.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <simple-id uuid='{8D7D3C73-8EF4-4857-9DD3-7BCE0806F128}' />
    </dashboard>
  </dashboards>
